sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-033: Chat Report, Review, and Action — Sequence Diagram
    actor PART as Eligible PART
    actor ADMIN as Platform ADMIN
    participant UI as React UI
    participant API as Express API + Guards
    participant MOD as Moderation Services
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / Supabase

    PART->>UI: Report a message already visible in chat
    UI->>API: POST /api/reports with chat_message, id, category, explanation
    API->>API: Require Firebase auth, MFA, active verified PART
    API->>MOD: Validate report input and message visibility
    MOD->>DB: Resolve chat_messages row and persisted channel
    alt Public channel or Confirmed member of linked team
        MOD->>DB: Create moderation_report and link existing Open case or create one
        DB-->>MOD: report_id, case_id, UTC created_at
        MOD-->>UI: Minimal Received receipt
        UI-->>PART: Confirmation only
    else Missing, private, unrelated, or direct-message identifier
        MOD-->>UI: Generic unavailable response without message content
        UI-->>PART: Safe error
    end
    Note over PART,MOD: Reporting grants no additional read access and never returns other reports, ADMIN notes, or action records.

    ADMIN->>UI: Open existing moderation safety queue
    UI->>API: GET moderation cases / selected case
    API->>API: Require Firebase auth, MFA, active stored ADMIN role
    API->>MOD: Load case and resolve polymorphic target
    MOD->>DB: Resolve target_type + target_id against matching chat table
    alt Target is available
        DB-->>MOD: Narrow channel or targeted-message evidence row
        MOD->>MOD: Project handle, UTC time, and redacted bounded context
        MOD-->>UI: Case plus privacy-safe evidence
        UI-->>ADMIN: Render safe chat context
    else Target is stale or missing
        DB-->>MOD: No target row
        MOD-->>UI: Case plus Unavailable target marker
        UI-->>ADMIN: Render stale-target state
    end

    ADMIN->>UI: Dismiss Open chat case with reason
    UI->>API: POST case decision
    API->>MOD: Recheck ADMIN, Open status, action, and reason
    alt Invalid, closed, or unsupported content-changing action
        MOD-->>UI: Safe validation or conflict response
        UI-->>ADMIN: Keep reason and show error
    else Valid dismissal
        MOD->>DB: Insert append-only event_action_records row
        MOD->>DB: Mark case Dismissed with UTC resolution time
        DB-->>MOD: Updated case and action history
        MOD-->>UI: Scrubbed outcome and safe state summary
        UI-->>ADMIN: Success notice and refreshed case
    end
    Note over API,DB: No endpoint returns credentials, OTPs, emails, tokens, or unrelated conversation history.

